SUMMARY:Deadline: Stroom Den Haag: PRO Art Projects
DESCRIPTION:Stroom Den Haag's PRO Art Projects scheme contributes to the co
 sts of realising a contemporary art project. WHO CAN APPLY: artists\, cura
 tors\, critics\, publicists\, partnerships and organisations.\n\nOrganisat
 ion: Stroom Den Haag\nLocation: The Hague\, Netherlands. Open to applicant
 s from outside The Hague (apply with a CV) as long as the project takes pl
 ace in The Hague or otherwise benefits art and artists in The Hague\; Hagu
 e artists must be registered in the Stroom database (Mijn Stroom).\nAward:
  Maximum EUR 10\,000 per project\, up to EUR 20\,000 per applicant per cal
 endar year. Requests above EUR 5\,000 require at least 30 percent co-finan
 cing of the total budget from third parties. Artist fees\, production and 
 communication costs are eligible\; Stroom endorses the kunstenaarshonorari
 um.nl fee guideline. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\; the gr
 ant remains valid for up to two years after the decision meeting\, with 80
  percent paid upfront and 20 percent on the final report\n\nMore: https://
 www.stroom.nl/en/stroom-for-artists/financial-support/pro-art-projects?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stroom.nl/en/stroom-for-artists/financial-support/pro-art-p
 rojects?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Hague\, Netherlands. Open to applicants from outside The Hague
  (apply with a CV) as long as the project takes place in The Hague or othe
 rwise benefits art and artists in The Hague\; Hague artists must be regist
 ered in the Stroom database (Mijn Stroom).
END:VEVENT
